      en: "The Port of Gioia Tauro in Calabria is the largest container terminal in Italy and one of the most significant transshipment hubs in the Mediterranean Sea. Originally conceived in the 1970s for a heavy industrial complex that was never realized, the port was repurposed in the 1990s into a state-of-the-art logistics center. Its strategic location along the Suez-Gibraltar shipping route makes it a vital nexus for global trade between Asia, Europe, and the Americas. The port features over 3.4 kilometers of quay and a draught of 18 meters, allowing it to accommodate the world's largest ultra-large container vessels. It serves as a crucial economic engine for Calabria and Southern Italy, providing thousands of jobs and integrating the region into international supply chains. In recent years, significant investments have been made in rail connectivity and automation to enhance efficiency and competitiveness. Gioia Tauro remains a cornerstone of Italy's maritime infrastructure and a key player in global shipping logistics.",
